<%# What sits where the composer would be when the conversation's SUBJECT
    has locked it (Chats::ChatSubject#chat_locked?). It carries the same DOM
    id as the composer's dock, so MessagesController#create can swap one for
    the other with a single Turbo replace when a thread closes under an open
    composer — the host's composer_actions leave with it.

    The `locked_composer` slot replaces the BODY (a reopen button, a link to
    the closed ticket…) while keeping the id contract intact.

    `notice:` replaces the subject's reason: the thread renders this same
    box, with "You can't message this person.", for a direct thread the
    host's policy no longer allows (or whose other account is gone). %>
<% notice = local_assigns[:notice] || conversation.locked_notice %>
<div id="<%= dom_id(conversation, :composer) %>" class="chats-composer chats-composer--locked">
  <% if chats_slot?(:locked_composer) %>
    <%= chats_slot :locked_composer, conversation: conversation, notice: notice %>
  <% else %>
    <p class="chats-composer__locked-notice"><%= notice %></p>
  <% end %>
</div>
